WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.950
Now the how.

2
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:05.550
The Group Policy sunset runs one
setting and one population at a time.

3
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.175
Every setting gets asked, in
order: is it still needed?

4
00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.250
Is there a direct Intune equivalent?

5
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.275
Does a cloud service replace the need, the
way OneDrive replaces redirected folders?

6
00:00:16.275 --> 00:00:17.750
Can a script enforce it?

7
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.112
Anything that fails all four becomes
a dated exception with an owner.

8
00:00:22.112 --> 00:00:26.577
Then the rules that keep it honest:
retire before you translate, one owner

9
00:00:26.577 --> 00:00:31.338
per setting, and no GPO link switched
off until its replacement shows success.

10
00:00:31.338 --> 00:00:35.887
GPOs are disabled first and kept
ninety days as a safety net.

11
00:00:35.887 --> 00:00:39.203
The decision for the
endpoint engineering lead:

12
00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:43.513
freeze every inventoried GPO, so
new requirements go to Intune.

13
00:00:43.513 --> 00:00:45.020
Next, the timeline.
